WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.094
This is the Energy Management Division Digital Platform,

2
00:00:07.094 --> 00:00:10.918
from the National Cleaner Production Centre, Sri Lanka.

3
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:16.491
Seven energy audit tools, in one place, on your phone and on your computer.

4
00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:20.324
Open the platform with the access code.

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:25.437
Each tool then asks for its own app code, so your work stays protected.

6
00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:30.384
First, LuxLog, the lighting survey app.

7
00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:34.740
Sketch each room, tap where you measured, and type the lux reading.

8
00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:43.388
Every reading is checked against the JIS Z9110 range and the OSHA minimum.

9
00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:47.170
You see at once which areas are good, low or high.

10
00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:52.011
The lux map colours the floor, to show the bright and the dark areas.

11
00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:56.538
Then see the whole room in 3D, with the furniture,

12
00:00:56.538 --> 00:00:59.177
the lights and every reading in place.

13
00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:05.654
LuxLog writes the Word report and the Excel workbook for you,

14
00:01:05.654 --> 00:01:08.915
with a drawing and a table for every section.

15
00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:16.322
Next, the calculators. Each one is built from the division's own Excel workbook,

16
00:01:16.322 --> 00:01:18.518
and follows the same formulas.

17
00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:23.590
Rooftop solar. Size the system, and see the generation,

18
00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:27.614
the cost saving, the payback and the net present value.

19
00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:33.187
Boiler efficiency, by the indirect method, with every loss shown.

20
00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:36.670
Air compressor replacement savings.

21
00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:41.415
And air conditioning savings, from inverter and VRF units.

22
00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:46.927
Change a highlighted box, and every result updates instantly.

23
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.964
Critical inputs are marked with a star, and

24
00:01:49.964 --> 00:01:53.494
model checks confirm that the numbers are consistent.

25
00:01:54.533 --> 00:01:59.118
The sub-meter verification report compares each meter with the logger,

26
00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:01.803
and flags every error outside your limit.

27
00:02:01.967 --> 00:02:05.692
Add photos, the calibration sheet and your signature.

28
00:02:06.733 --> 00:02:11.626
The Smart ESO Sheet lists every energy saving opportunity, with

29
00:02:11.626 --> 00:02:16.519
the cost and greenhouse gas saving worked out for each measure.

30
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:22.241
And it works like Excel. Type equals, click the cells, and the formula is built.

31
00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.524
Copy, paste, fill and undo all work too.

32
00:02:26.867 --> 00:02:33.937
When you finish, the Download buttons at the top right give you the Word report and the Excel workbook,

33
00:02:33.937 --> 00:02:34.898
ready to send.

34
00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:38.455
Your work is saved on your own device as you type.

35
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.571
The Energy Management Division Digital Platform.

36
00:02:43.733 --> 00:02:47.061
Developed by Vihindu Jayawardena.
